# The subject is pci-scan-all's bridge-descent branch, which cannot run without
# a PCI-to-PCI bridge on the bus. -pci-bridge puts one on bus 0 forwarding to
# bus 1 with an endpoint (1af4:1041) behind it. Calibrated by sabotage: with the
# flag the scan descends and reports bus1=1 (count 5); WITHOUT it there is no
# bridge, the descent branch cannot execute, and the same binary reports
# bus1=0 (count 3). The flag moves the row, so the descent is load-bearing.
-pci-bridge
